Star catalogue data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Yale Bright Star Catalogue, 5th Revised Edition (BSC5)
Hoffleit, D. and Warren, W. H., 1991
Yale University Observatory

The catalogue is a scientific data set in the public domain. The copy used here
was taken from the JSON mirror at
https://github.com/brettonw/YaleBrightStarCatalog (bsc5-all.json).

star-data/stars.json is a derived subset of that catalogue, keeping ten fields
per star: name, designation, constellation, apparent magnitude, distance in
light-years, spectral class, right ascension, declination, colour temperature
and a short flavour line. No values were altered; fields were dropped, and
distances were converted from arcseconds of parallax to light-years.

The page credits the source in its legend: "star data: yale bright star
catalogue".
